{"q":{"id":"Q01","question":"How is the Conflict deck built, and what happens to unused Conflict cards?"},"key":{"id":"Q01","expected_answer":"Shuffle all four III cards at the bottom, five randomly dealt of nine II cards above, one randomly dealt of three I cards on top: ten total. Return unused cards to the box without looking.","source_references":"Main PDF p4 / extraction 190–209","novelty":"Conflict deck construction"},"A":{"id":"Q01","answer":"Shuffle all 4 Conflict III cards and place them face down at the bottom; shuffle 9 Conflict II cards and deal 5 above them; shuffle 3 Conflict I cards and deal 1 on top. This makes a face-down 10-card deck. Return unused Conflict cards to the box without looking at them.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: “face-down 10-card Conflict Deck”"},"B":{"id":"Q01","answer":"Shuffle all 4 III cards and place them face down at the bottom; shuffle all 9 II cards and deal 5 face down above them; shuffle all 3 I cards and deal 1 face down on top. Return unused I and II cards to the box unseen.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: “shuffle…deal”; return unused Conflict cards unseen."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q02","question":"What are the starting score, Agents, troops and water for a human in a four-player game versus a three-player game?"},"key":{"id":"Q02","expected_answer":"Four players start at 1 VP; three at 0. Each has two Agents on Leader and third beside board, three troops in garrison with remaining nine in supply, and one water.","source_references":"Main pp4–5 / extraction 254–303","novelty":"Player setup"},"A":{"id":"Q02","answer":"Four-player human: start at 1 VP; three-player human: start at 0 VP. Both start with two Agents on the Leader and the third (Swordmaster) beside the board; three troops in their nearest garrison and nine in supply; and 1 water.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: “Score marker—on 1 for a four-player game, otherwise on 0”; “two Agents”; “three…garrison…remaining nine”; “Take 1 water.”"},"B":{"id":"Q02","answer":"Four-player human: score marker starts at 1; three-player: 0. Both start with 2 Agents on the Leader and the third (Swordmaster) beside the board; 3 troops in the nearest garrison and 9 in supply; 1 water.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, step 6; Human component layout."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q03","question":"Can you Reveal with Agents left, and can you later take an Agent turn in the same round? What cards supply Reveal effects and where do all played cards go?"},"key":{"id":"Q03","expected_answer":"May Reveal early; no more turns this phase after Reveal. Only cards remaining in hand and just revealed supply Reveal effects, not Agent-turn cards. Clean Up puts all Agent and Reveal cards in discard pile.","source_references":"Main pp8,12 / extraction 360–379,637–673","novelty":"Reveal commitment and destinations"},"A":{"id":"Q03","answer":"Yes, you may take a Reveal turn while Agents remain; after Revealing, your turns are skipped for the rest of Player Turns. Reveal effects come only from cards revealed in the Reveal turn, not cards played on Agent turns. Clean Up moves all cards in front of you (Agent and Reveal turns) to your discard pile.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Reveal turn may be taken early; “Resolve Reveal Effects”; “Clean Up”"},"B":{"id":"Q03","answer":"Yes, you may Reveal while Agents remain, and after Revealing your turns are skipped for the rest of Player Turns. Reveal effects come only from cards revealed then, not Agent-turn cards. At Clean Up all cards in front of you, from both Agent and Reveal turns, go to your discard pile.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Player Turns; Reveal Turn."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q04","question":"May an Agent-turn card effect provide resources to pay the destination entry cost? How many Agents can one card send, and can a card without Agent icons be used?"},"key":{"id":"Q04","expected_answer":"Entry costs paid immediately before any card or space effects; cannot use later gains to pay entry. One card sends one Agent using one matching icon. No-icon card cannot be played on an Agent turn.","source_references":"Main p9 / extraction 425–452","novelty":"Entry legality and costs"},"A":{"id":"Q04","answer":"No: entry costs must be paid immediately before resolving effects from the destination or the played Agent card, so those later resources cannot pay that entry. One card sends only one Agent, using one chosen Agent icon. A card without Agent icons cannot be used for an Agent turn; it may be revealed.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Agent Turn entry-cost timing; “You choose only one Agent icon”; “no Agent icons”"},"B":{"id":"Q04","answer":"No: the entry cost must be payable immediately before resolving destination or played-card effects, so Agent-box gains cannot pay it. One card sends one Agent using one matching icon. A card with no Agent icons cannot be used on an Agent turn.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Agent Turn; entry-cost timing."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q05","question":"At a Combat space you recruit three troops this turn and already have four garrisoned. How many can deploy? What if the destination is not a Combat space, and where do recruited troops originate?"},"key":{"id":"Q05","expected_answer":"May deploy all three newly recruited plus at most two older garrison troops, five total. Normal deployment unavailable at noncombat space. Recruit from own supply into garrison; empty supply prevents recruiting.","source_references":"Main p10 / extraction 535–566","novelty":"Recruit and deployment limits"},"A":{"id":"Q05","answer":"At a Combat space, deploy all three troops recruited this turn plus up to two from the garrison: five total in this example. A non-Combat space does not permit normal deployment. Recruits come from your supply into your garrison; at a Combat space, recruited this turn may then deploy.","support":"supported","evidence":"Recruiting & Deploying Units: “any or all units recruited during your current turn…plus up to two more”"},"B":{"id":"Q05","answer":"You may deploy the 3 troops recruited this turn plus up to 2 from the garrison: at most 5 total in this example. At a non-Combat destination, you cannot deploy; recruited troops go to your garrison. Troops are recruited from your personal supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"Actions: Recruiting & Deploying Units."}}

