{"q":{"id":"Q06","question":"How do you use a Spy Agent icon, Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence? Can the same Spy pay for both, and when must Gather Intelligence be chosen?"},"key":{"id":"Q06","expected_answer":"Spy Agent icon permits a connected space without recalling Spy. Infiltrate recalls own connected Spy to bypass another player Agent. Gather Intelligence recalls own connected Spy to draw, chosen immediately after placement before card/space effects. Same Spy cannot do both; separate Spies can.","source_references":"Main p11 / extraction 606–622","novelty":"Distinct spy functions and timing"},"A":{"id":"Q06","answer":"A Spy Agent icon permits sending an Agent to a space connected to an observation post where your Spy currently sits; you do not recall that Spy. Infiltrate recalls your Spy at a connected post to bypass another player’s Agent, not your own. Gather Intelligence recalls a connected Spy for one card draw, chosen immediately after Agent placement and before any space/card effects. The same Spy cannot serve both abilities; two different Spies can serve Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence, but only one Gather Intelligence draw is allowed per placement.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: “Separate Spy costs and Spy Agent access”; “Gather Intelligence”"},"B":{"id":"Q06","answer":"A Spy Agent icon grants access to any board space connected to an observation post where you currently have a Spy; it does not recall that Spy. Infiltrate recalls your Spy from a connected post to bypass another player’s Agent, never your own. Gather Intelligence recalls a connected Spy to draw 1 card; choose immediately after placement and before space/card effects. The same Spy cannot pay both Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence; two different Spies may. Only one Gather Intelligence draw per placement.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Spy Agent access, Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q07","question":"With two troops, one sandworm and four revealed swords, what is your strength? What if your final unit is removed? Can you participate in Combat Intrigue with no unit?"},"key":{"id":"Q07","expected_answer":"Strength 11 (2+2+3+4). No units means zero strength regardless swords. Without a unit cannot participate in Combat Intrigue.","source_references":"Main pp12,14 / extraction 652–665,744–750","novelty":"Strength and eligibility"},"A":{"id":"Q07","answer":"Strength is 2 troops × 2 + 1 sandworm × 3 + 4 swords = 11. If your final unit is removed, your strength becomes 0. You cannot play Combat Intrigue without at least one unit in the Conflict.","support":"supported","evidence":"Strength: troop 2, sandworm 3, sword 1; “if your last unit is ever removed”; Intrigue cards"},"B":{"id":"Q07","answer":"Strength is 11: two troops = 4, one sandworm = 3, four revealed swords = 4. If your final unit is removed, strength becomes 0. You cannot play Combat Intrigue without at least one unit in the Conflict.","support":"supported","evidence":"Actions: Strength; Phase 3 Combat Intrigue."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q08","question":"If you pass Combat Intrigue and an opponent then plays one, may you act again? When does the window close, and where do troops and sandworms go after rewards?"},"key":{"id":"Q08","expected_answer":"May act again after earlier pass; closes only when all involved players pass consecutively. Adjust strength for effects. After all rewards troops return to supply not garrison, sandworms to bank, Combat markers reset zero.","source_references":"Main p14 / extraction 744–750,767–769","novelty":"Combat priority and cleanup"},"A":{"id":"Q08","answer":"Yes. Passing earlier does not prevent acting again if an opponent later plays; the window closes after all players involved in Combat pass consecutively. After rewards, troops return to each player's supply (not garrison), Combat markers reset to 0, and sandworms return to the bank.","support":"supported","evidence":"Combat: “not required to pass just because you passed earlier”; cleanup"},"B":{"id":"Q08","answer":"Yes. Passing is not binding if another player later plays; the window closes after all involved players pass consecutively. After rewards, troops return to supply (not garrison), sandworms to the bank.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 3: Combat."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q09","question":"Compare two players tied for first in a four-player Conflict with the same tie in a three-player Conflict. Who takes the Conflict card, and can a zero-strength player get a reward?"},"key":{"id":"Q09","expected_answer":"Each tied first gets second reward and nobody wins or takes card. In four-player game remaining players compete for third; in three-player game no further rewards. Zero strength never rewarded.","source_references":"Main p14 / extraction 765,792–808","novelty":"Tie for first outcome branches"},"A":{"id":"Q09","answer":"With two tied for first in four-player play, each gets the second reward; the remaining players compete for the third reward. Nobody wins the Conflict or takes its card. The same tie in a three-player game gives each tied player the second reward, no other reward, and nobody takes the card. A zero-strength player receives no reward.","support":"supported","evidence":"Combat ties: “Exactly two tied first”; “A player with 0 strength receives no reward.”"},"B":{"id":"Q09","answer":"In both player counts, tied first players each get the second reward and nobody wins or takes the Conflict card. In four-player play, if exactly two tie first, the remaining players compete for third reward; in three-player play there are no other rewards. A zero-strength player receives none.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 3: Resolve Combat; Combat ties."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q10","question":"What does a sandworm do to rewards: do two sandworms quadruple them, can control or battle icons double, and how is a reward offering 3 spice for 1 VP handled?"},"key":{"id":"Q10","expected_answer":"One or more sandworms doubles, never quadruples. Control and battle icons do not double. Optional reward cost may be paid second time: 3 spice for 1 VP or 6 for 2, not free second VP.","source_references":"Main p14 / extraction 778–791","novelty":"Doubling scope and cost exception"},"A":{"id":"Q10","answer":"One or more sandworms double rewards; multiple worms do not multiply beyond doubling. Control of a location and battle icons on Conflict cards cannot be doubled. For a reward offering 3 spice to gain 1 VP, you may pay 3 spice once for 1 VP, or pay the cost a second time (6 spice total) to gain 2 VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Sandworm Reward Doubling: “one or more”; exceptions and optional reward example"},"B":{"id":"Q10","answer":"One or more sandworms double rewards once; multiple worms do not multiply further. Control and battle icons on won Conflict cards cannot be doubled. For a reward offering 3 spice to gain 1 VP, you may pay 3 spice once for 1 VP or pay 6 spice to take the doubled 2 VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Sandworm Reward Doubling."}}

