{"q":{"id":"Q11","question":"When is a normal battle-icon match checked, which cards qualify, is matching optional, and how is a wild icon used?"},"key":{"id":"Q11","expected_answer":"After winning and taking Conflict card face up in supply check another face-up Conflict or Objective with same icon; must flip pair face down for 1 VP. At Endgame wild can match any of three icons in supply, pair flipped for 1 VP.","source_references":"Main p14,p20 / extraction 770–777,1090–1096","novelty":"Battle icon match"},"A":{"id":"Q11","answer":"After winning and taking the Conflict card face up into your supply, check for a match against another face-up Conflict or Objective card in your supply. A match is mandatory: flip the pair face down and gain 1 VP. In the Endgame, a wild icon may match any one of the three battle icons in your supply, for the same 1 VP pair flip.","support":"supported","evidence":"Battle Icons: “must flip the matching pair”; Endgame wild match"},"B":{"id":"Q11","answer":"After winning and taking a Conflict card face up into your supply, check it against another face-up Conflict or Objective card in your supply. A matching pair must be flipped face down for 1 VP. During Endgame, a wild icon may match any one of the three icons in your supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"Resolve Combat winner procedure; Battle Icons."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q12","question":"What are the rewards and reversibility at 2 and 4 Faction Influence, and does tying the Alliance holder at 4 steal the Alliance?"},"key":{"id":"Q12","expected_answer":"Reach 2 gets 1 VP lost below 2. Reach 4 gets track bonus retained if falling below, can earn again on re-reaching. First to 4 gets Alliance and its VP; tie does not steal, opponent must rise higher. Transfer loses old holder VP and gives new holder VP.","source_references":"Main p7 / extraction 333–344","novelty":"Influence thresholds and Alliance"},"A":{"id":"Q12","answer":"At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP; falling below 2 loses it, and reaching 2 again regains it. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained if you fall below 4 and earned again on returning to 4. The first player to 4 also takes the Alliance and its 1 VP. Merely tying the Alliance holder does not steal it: you must rise above their Influence (or the separate FAQ holder-loses-Influence rule may transfer it).","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring: Faction Influence: “At 2 Influence”; “two separate rewards”; “tying…does not steal”"},"B":{"id":"Q12","answer":"At 2 Influence gain 1 VP; lose that VP below 2 and regain it on reaching 2 again. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, retain it if dropping below 4, and earn it again on returning to 4; the first to 4 gains the Alliance token and its 1 VP. Tying the holder does not take it: a challenger must rise above. FAQ also says a holder losing Influence after a tie transfers it to a formerly tied player (or chooses among tied players); at 3 or lower, if no one has 4+, it returns to board and holder loses its VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring: Faction Influence; FAQ: Alliance loss."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q13","question":"When can Persuasion be spent during Reveal, may it be pooled or split, can you buy a Row replacement immediately, and where does the acquired card go?"},"key":{"id":"Q13","expected_answer":"Before between or after Reveal effects; can pool and split. Refill Row to five immediately; may buy replacement with remaining Persuasion. Acquired card face-up discard, cannot use immediately; unspent Persuasion lost.","source_references":"Main pp12–13 / extraction 645–649,704–730","novelty":"Acquisition timing and destination"},"A":{"id":"Q13","answer":"During your Reveal turn, Persuasion may be spent before, between, or after Reveal effects. You may pool it across sources to buy one card or split one source across cards. After buying a Row card, refill the Row immediately and you may buy the replacement if you can afford it. Acquired cards go face up into your discard pile.","support":"supported","evidence":"Acquiring Cards: Reveal timing, pooling/splitting, Row refill, discard pile"},"B":{"id":"Q13","answer":"Spend Persuasion before, between, or after Reveal effects. Pool Persuasion across sources to buy one card, or split one source across cards. The Imperium Row refills to five, and you may buy a replacement immediately if you can afford it. Acquired cards go face up to your discard pile.","support":"supported","evidence":"Acquiring Cards."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q14","question":"How do Maker bonus spice, the Shield Wall and Maker Hooks affect harvesting and summoning, and where can a sandworm be placed?"},"key":{"id":"Q14","expected_answer":"Makers phase adds one bonus spice on each unoccupied Maker space, accumulating; visiting collects all bonus spice. Shield Wall blocks worms at Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, Imperial Basin until removed to box. Maker Hooks prerequisite when specified; summoning directly bank to Conflict, never garrison.","source_references":"Main pp10,15,20 / extraction 493–522,567–584,835–845,1130–1135","novelty":"Maker and worm restrictions"},"A":{"id":"Q14","answer":"A visit to a Maker space takes all bonus spice there. At Makers, an Agent-free space gets one additional spice during Makers phase. Deep Desert costs 3 water and Hagga Basin costs 1 water. Worm options require Maker Hooks; a protected Conflict at Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, or Imperial Basin cannot receive a summoned worm while the Shield Wall remains. The usual sandworm icon may require Hooks if printed as a condition, but Hooks are not universally required; they are retained, not spent. A sandworm can never go in a garrison, and cannot be summoned at those three protected Conflicts until the Wall is removed.","support":"supported","evidence":"Sandworms; Makers; Board Space Guide; Shield Wall"},"B":{"id":"Q14","answer":"At an unoccupied Maker space, add 1 spice to its bonus spot during Makers; visiting gains all bonus spice there. Deep Desert (3 water) offers 4 base spice or, with Hooks, 2 sandworms; Hagga Basin (1 water) offers 2 base spice or, with Hooks, 1 worm. Worms cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery or Imperial Basin while Shield Wall remains; removing it allows any Conflict. Hooks are required only when specified by the effect and are retained, not spent. Worms are placed directly in your Conflict quadrant, never garrison.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 4: Makers; Sandworms; Board Space Guide."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q15","question":"At what point does 10 VP or an empty Conflict deck end play, what happens before comparing final VP, and what are the rulebook resource tiebreakers?"},"key":{"id":"Q15","expected_answer":"Check in Recall at end of round, not immediately at 10 VP. Resolve Endgame Intrigue first then highest VP wins. Ties spice then Solari then water then garrisoned troops.","source_references":"Main pp15 / extraction 824–855","novelty":"End trigger and scoring"},"A":{"id":"Q15","answer":"Endgame triggers at the end of a round if any player has 10+ VP or the Conflict Deck is empty. Players first may play and resolve Endgame Intrigue; then compare VP. Tiebreakers are spice, then Solari, then water, then garrisoned troops.","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring / Victory Conditions: “At the end of a round”; Endgame Intrigue; tiebreakers"},"B":{"id":"Q15","answer":"At the end of a round, 10+ VP by any player or an empty Conflict Deck triggers Endgame. Players first may play and resolve Endgame Intrigues, then compare VP. Tiebreakers are spice, Solari, water, garrisoned troops, in that order.","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring / Victory Conditions."}}

