{"q":{"id":"Q16","question":"With optional standard CHOAM, how many contracts start face up and face down, which extra cards are added, is Shaddam compulsory, and are the 10 contrasting-back contracts part of this standard setup?"},"key":{"id":"Q16","expected_answer":"20 standard contracts: two face up, eighteen in bank. Add four Intrigue and four Imperium; Shaddam optional. Ten contrasting-back contracts are only Rise of Ix compatibility, excluded from standard setup.","source_references":"Main p16 / extraction 860–879,916–936","novelty":"CHOAM setup and compatibility boundary"},"A":{"id":"Q16","answer":"Standard CHOAM starts with two face-up contracts and 18 face-down in the bank. Add four CHOAM Imperium cards and four CHOAM Intrigue cards to their respective decks. Shaddam is optional. The 10 contrasting-back contracts belong to Rise of Ix compatibility and are left out of standard CHOAM.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM Module: Setup changes; “20 standard contracts”; contrasting-back set"},"B":{"id":"Q16","answer":"CHOAM is optional and Shaddam is optional. Shuffle 20 standard contracts and reveal 2 face up; the other 18 are face down in the bank. Add 4 Intrigue and 4 Imperium cards. The 10 contrasting-back contracts are Rise of Ix compatibility only and stay boxed.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM Module; Setup changes."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q17","question":"Under CHOAM, what does the contract icon do, what if all contracts are taken, and how are Harvest, Immediate and Acquire The Spice Must Flow contracts completed?"},"key":{"id":"Q17","expected_answer":"With CHOAM, take one of the available face-up contracts on the board into your supply, then replace it face up from the bank if a bank contract remains. The printed icon guide gives 2 Solari if there are none left; this does not require every contract token in the game to have been acquired. In particular, another human with no public contract available gains 2 Solari even if Shaddam's set-aside Sardaukar contracts remain unacquired, and cannot take those reserved contracts. Without CHOAM the icon also gives 2 Solari. Shaddam's own reserved-contract option follows Sardaukar Commander and the FAQ. A Harvest contract completes by sending an Agent to a Maker space and gaining the specified total spice during that turn, including other sources. Immediate completes as soon as taken. Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when that card is next acquired.","source_references":"See benchmark-v17/source-reference-appendix.json: original main PDF pp16,20, Uprising Board Space Guide, original Shaddam Leader and official FAQ p3, exact named-file/hash locators.","novelty":"CHOAM taking and types"},"A":{"id":"Q17","answer":"With CHOAM, take a face-up public contract and refill its offer face up from the bank if possible; if none are face up, gain 2 Solari. Harvest completes by sending an Agent to a Maker space and gaining the contract’s spice amount that turn in total, including other sources. Immediate completes when taken. Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM Module: Taking contracts; Completing contracts"},"B":{"id":"Q17","answer":"With CHOAM, take a public face-up contract and refill from the bank if possible; if public offers are exhausted, gain 2 Solari (even if Shaddam’s reserved contracts remain). Harvest completes by visiting a Maker space and gaining the pictured spice amount total from all sources that turn; Immediate completes upon taking it; Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM: Taking contracts; Completing contracts."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q18","question":"You gain a board-space contract after already sending your Agent to that space this turn. Can you complete it now? Once completed what do you announce, gain and do with the token?"},"key":{"id":"Q18","expected_answer":"Cannot complete now; must have held contract when Agent sent, wait future turn. Announce completion, gain printed rewards, flip face down and leave in supply.","source_references":"Main p16 / extraction 902–907","novelty":"CHOAM ownership timing and destination"},"A":{"id":"Q18","answer":"No. If you take a contract for a board space where you already sent your Agent this turn, you must wait for a future turn; you must hold the contract when sending the Agent. On completion, announce it, gain its shown rewards, then flip it face down and leave it in your supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM Module: Completing contracts"},"B":{"id":"Q18","answer":"No; a space contract can only be completed on a future turn if acquired after you already placed your Agent there, because you must hold it when sending the Agent. On completion, announce it, gain its rewards, then flip it face down and leave it in your supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM: Completing contracts; FAQ: Contract completion."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q19","question":"In standard two-player play how many Rivals are used, who gets the Ornithopter Objective, who gets First Player, what is the turn order, and does a Rival Reveal?"},"key":{"id":"Q19","expected_answer":"One shared Rival. Rival gets Ornithopter Objective, other two randomly humans; Rival never First Player. Marker alternates humans, Rival considered clockwise from First Player and acts between humans each round. Takes Agent turns while it has Agent in supply, never Reveals.","source_references":"Supplements PDF pp3–4","novelty":"Required two-player setup and turn order"},"A":{"id":"Q19","answer":"Use one shared scoring Rival as the third competitor. It gets the Ornithopter Objective; humans randomly receive the other two eligible Objectives, and the human with the First Player marker on their Objective goes first. Turn order begins First Player → Rival → other human. The Rival takes Agent turns while it has Agents and never Reveals.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup; Agent turns"},"B":{"id":"Q19","answer":"One shared scoring Rival is the third competitor. It receives the Ornithopter Objective; deal the other two eligible Objectives randomly to humans. First Player is the human whose Objective shows the marker; Rival is immediately clockwise, so order is First Player → Rival → other human. Rival never Reveals.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup; Agent turns."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q20","question":"A Rival reveals an occupied board space, then a Place Spy card. How does it proceed, which space costs and effects apply, and what happens when House Hagal is empty or Reshuffle is drawn?"},"key":{"id":"Q20","expected_answer":"Occupied: ignore and reveal again. Place Spy tries empty designated post, ignore placement if none, then reveal another card regardless because no Agent sent. Ignore normal space costs/effects; use Hagal effects only. Empty deck or Reshuffle: immediately reshuffle Hagal and continue.","source_references":"Supplements PDF p4","novelty":"Rival card resolution"},"A":{"id":"Q20","answer":"Ignore an occupied destination and reveal another Hagal card; Place Spy cards do not place an Agent, so attempt an empty post of the specified type, then immediately reveal another Hagal card whether placement succeeded or not. Rival ignores ordinary board-space costs/effects and applies only Hagal effects (including its resource, Influence, Signet, troop, Spy and Hooks icons). If Hagal empties or Reshuffle appears, immediately reshuffle and continue.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns; Place Spy cards; ignore normal space costs/effects; Reshuffle"},"B":{"id":"Q20","answer":"For an occupied destination, ignore it and reveal again. A Place Spy card does not place an Agent: try its specified empty post; if none, ignore placement; either way reveal another Hagal card and continue the Agent turn. Ignore normal space costs/effects, applying only Hagal effects. If Hagal empties or Reshuffle appears, immediately reshuffle and continue.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns; Place Spy cards."}}

