{"q":{"id":"Q21","question":"How are eligible Objective cards selected and distributed in standard three- or four-player setup, how is First Player chosen, and may Shaddam be chosen without CHOAM?"},"key":{"id":"Q21","expected_answer":"Omit Objectives whose 1–3P or 4/6P mark mismatches count; shuffle, each takes one random face up in supply. First Player is holder of marked Objective. Shaddam cannot be chosen without CHOAM.","source_references":"Main pp4–5 / extraction 210–220,254–263","novelty":"Objective eligibility and Leader restriction"},"A":{"id":"Q21","answer":"Omit Objective cards marked for a different player count, shuffle eligible cards, and give each player one random Objective face up. Its First Player marker identifies the first player. Shaddam may be used only with the CHOAM Module.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: Objective cards; Shaddam setup restriction"},"B":{"id":"Q21","answer":"Shuffle Objectives after omitting cards whose 1–3P/4/6P marking does not match; distribute one eligible card face up to each player. Its First Player marker selects the first player. Shaddam may be used only with CHOAM.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, steps 3 and 5."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q22","question":"If the bank runs out of Solari, spice, water or sandworms, what happens? Contrast an empty personal troop supply, and state where resource payments go."},"key":{"id":"Q22","expected_answer":"Bank resources and sandworms not limited; substitute conveniently. Cannot recruit troops from empty personal supply until returned. Resource gains come from bank and payments return to bank.","source_references":"Main pp5,10,20 / extraction 273–279,535–539,1152–1154","novelty":"Component exhaustion and bank destinations"},"A":{"id":"Q22","answer":"Solari, spice and water tokens and sandworms are not meant to be limited; make convenient substitutions if the bank runs out. An empty personal troop supply means you cannot recruit more until troops return to it. Resource payments go back to the common bank.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: “These are not meant to be limited”; Recruiting; bank rule"},"B":{"id":"Q22","answer":"Bank resources and sandworms are not limited: make any convenient substitution if they run out. If your personal troop supply is empty, you cannot recruit more until troops return there. Gains come from the bank and payments return to the bank.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, step 7; Recruiting & Deploying Units."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q23","question":"State all five round phases in order, when Conflict and hand cards are drawn, and what Recall does if Endgame is not triggered."},"key":{"id":"Q23","expected_answer":"Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. Start reveals top Conflict face up atop previous remaining cards then each draws five. If no Endgame, recall Agents to Leaders, pass First Player clockwise and begin next round (two-player Rival exception).","source_references":"Main pp8,15 / extraction 355–360,385–390,824–834","novelty":"Round order and restart"},"A":{"id":"Q23","answer":"The five phases are Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. At Round Start reveal the next Conflict, resolve any defensive troop bonus, then each player draws five cards. If Recall does not trigger Endgame, humans return Agents to Leaders; in 3–4 human play pass First Player clockwise, while in two-player play return Rival Agents to supply and pass First Player to the other human.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure; Recall"},"B":{"id":"Q23","answer":"The five phases are Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. Round Start reveals a Conflict, resolves controlled-location defense, then each player draws 5. If Recall does not trigger Endgame, human Agents return to Leaders; First Player passes clockwise with 3–4 humans. In two-player, Rival Agents return to supply and First Player passes to the other human.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure; Phase 5: Recall."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q24","question":"May you resolve board-space effects, Agent-box effects and Faction Influence in any order? Can you use that visit’s Influence to meet its entry requirement?"},"key":{"id":"Q24","expected_answer":"Resolve effects in any order after placement, but entry requirements and costs must be met before any effects. Cannot rely on Influence gained by the visit for its entry requirement.","source_references":"Main p9 / extraction 403–409,439–452,482–489","novelty":"Effect-order versus entry requirement priority"},"A":{"id":"Q24","answer":"Yes, after paying entry costs and meeting requirements first, you may resolve the board-space effects, Agent-box effects and Faction Influence in any order. Therefore the Influence from that visit cannot satisfy that visit’s entry requirement.","support":"supported","evidence":"Agent Turn: pay before effects; “may carry out all these effects in any order.”"},"B":{"id":"Q24","answer":"Yes, board-space effects, Agent-box effects, and Faction advancement may be resolved in any order. No, entry requirements and costs must be met before effects resolve, so the visit’s Influence cannot meet its own entry requirement.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Agent Turn; Influence-requirement spaces."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q25","question":"Can an optional arrow cost be paid twice in an Agent turn? Which effects are normally optional or mandatory, including costs on Intrigue cards?"},"key":{"id":"Q25","expected_answer":"Only once per turn, except sandworm-doubled Conflict rewards. Most effects mandatory except may, optional arrow payment and black-X trash. Direct self-trash mandatory. All Intrigue conditions/costs required to play it.","source_references":"Main pp9,20; FAQ p3 optional effects/paying a cost","novelty":"Optional effect boundary and Intrigue exception"},"A":{"id":"Q25","answer":"An optional arrow cost/effect may be paid only once per turn; do not repeat it to multiply its effect. Most card and space effects are mandatory. Effects marked “may,” arrow costs, and the black-X trash icon are optional; a direct instruction to trash itself is mandatory. Intrigue costs and conditions must be met to play it.","support":"supported","evidence":"Arrows / paying costs; FAQ: Mandatory effects and costs"},"B":{"id":"Q25","answer":"An optional arrow cost/effect may be paid only once per turn, not twice (sandworm reward doubling is the exception). Most card/space effects are mandatory; “may,” optional arrow costs, and black-X trash are exceptions. Intrigue play still requires meeting its conditions and paying all its costs.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Arrows / paying costs; FAQ: Mandatory effects and costs."}}

