{"q":{"id":"Q31","question":"When can Plot, Combat and Endgame Intrigues be played, how are unplayed Intrigues kept and ordinary ones discarded, and what if the Intrigue deck is exhausted?"},"key":{"id":"Q31","expected_answer":"Plot during own Agent/Reveal turns, Combat during Combat with a unit, Endgame at game end. Unplayed face down separate from deck, owner may inspect; played resolved cards face up Intrigue discard. Exhaustion reshuffles Intrigue discard into new deck.","source_references":"Main p7 / extraction 345–354; FAQ p2 Intrigue cards","novelty":"Intrigue storage, timing and exhaustion"},"A":{"id":"Q31","answer":"Plot Intrigues may be played on your Agent or Reveal turn; Combat Intrigues during Combat if you have at least one unit in the Conflict; Endgame Intrigues at game end. Keep unplayed Intrigues face down separate from your deck; after resolving, discard them face up beside the Intrigue Deck. If its draw deck runs out, shuffle its discard into a new deck.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Intrigue cards; FAQ Draw timing"},"B":{"id":"Q31","answer":"Plot Intrigues: own Agent or Reveal turns; Combat Intrigues: Combat only and only with a unit in Conflict; Endgame Intrigues: at game end. Keep Intrigues face down, separate from deck; after resolving, face up in discard. If deck empties, shuffle its discard into a new deck.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Intrigue cards; FAQ: Draw timing."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q32","question":"Can you discard an Intrigue for an ordinary discard instruction? Where does an ordinary discard come from? How does Secrets choose which Intrigue is stolen?"},"key":{"id":"Q32","expected_answer":"Ordinary discard from hand and cannot be Intrigue unless specified. Secrets steals one random Intrigue from each opponent with four or more, in addition to drawing one from deck and gaining Bene Gesserit Influence.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1179–1181; Supplements p2; FAQ p2 discard","novelty":"Discard type and theft threshold"},"A":{"id":"Q32","answer":"An ordinary discard instruction discards a chosen card from your hand and cannot discard an Intrigue unless specified. The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes an Intrigue of your choice from your hand. Secrets steals one Intrigue at random from each opponent who has four or more Intrigue cards.","support":"supported","evidence":"Discarding; Trashing; Intrigue cards"},"B":{"id":"Q32","answer":"An ordinary discard is a card of your choice from your hand, not an Intrigue unless specified. Secrets’ Steal Intrigue makes each opponent with 4+ Intrigues give one selected at random. The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon lets you trash one Intrigue of your choice from hand.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Discarding; Intrigue cards."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q33","question":"Which cards may a trash effect remove, where do ordinary and Reserve cards go, and is trashing optional? Does trashing The Spice Must Flow remove its acquired VP?"},"key":{"id":"Q33","expected_answer":"May trash own hand, discard or in-play card. Ordinary to box; Reserve back to its Reserve stack. Optional unless cost or direct self-trash. The Spice Must Flow acquire VP retained after trashing.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1185–1190; FAQ p4 The Spice Must Flow","novelty":"Trash locations and persistent acquire VP"},"A":{"id":"Q33","answer":"Trash effects can remove cards from your hand, discard pile or in play. Return trashed cards to the box; Reserve cards return to their Reserve stack. Trashing is optional unless it pays a cost or a card directs you to trash itself. The Spice Must Flow acquire VP remains even if the card is later trashed.","support":"supported","evidence":"Trashing; FAQ Victory"},"B":{"id":"Q33","answer":"Trash effects can remove cards from hand, discard pile, or in play; ordinary cards return to the box and Reserve cards return to their Reserve stack. Trashing is optional unless paying a cost or instructed to trash itself. The Spice Must Flow acquire VP remains even if the card is later trashed.","support":"supported","evidence":"Actions: Trashing; FAQ: Victory."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q34","question":"When do acquire-box effects resolve, when do you reshuffle your deck, and can unused Persuasion be carried to another round?"},"key":{"id":"Q34","expected_answer":"Acquire effect once at acquisition not when later played. Reshuffle discard only when unable to draw due to empty deck then continue. Unspent Reveal Persuasion lost, never saved.","source_references":"Main pp6,13,20 / extraction 311–317,704–730,1081–1084","novelty":"Acquire triggers, reshuffle trigger and resource expiration"},"A":{"id":"Q34","answer":"An acquire-box effect resolves once when you acquire that card. If you cannot draw because your deck is empty, reshuffle your discard pile into a new deck and continue drawing. Unused Persuasion is lost at the end of Reveal and cannot carry over.","support":"supported","evidence":"Acquire box; Acquiring Cards"},"B":{"id":"Q34","answer":"Acquire-box effects resolve once when acquiring the card, not when playing it. If your deck is empty when drawing, shuffle your discard pile into a new deck and continue. Unused Persuasion is lost at the end of Reveal and cannot carry forward.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Acquire box; Acquiring Cards."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q35","question":"What counts as in play for Fremen Bond, can two Bond cards activate one another regardless of play order, and when do they cease being in play?"},"key":{"id":"Q35","expected_answer":"Agent-turn and Reveal cards remain in play face up until Reveal Clean Up unless trashed earlier. Bond requires at least one other Fremen in play; two Bond cards can activate each other regardless of order.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1111–1117","novelty":"In-play lifetime and Fremen Bond interaction"},"A":{"id":"Q35","answer":"Cards played on Agent turns and cards revealed on Reveal turns remain in play until Clean Up (unless trashed first). Fremen Bond can use one or more other Fremen cards in play; two Bond cards may activate each other regardless of order played. Clean Up ends that in-play status by moving the cards to discard.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: In play / Fremen Bond"},"B":{"id":"Q35","answer":"Cards played on Agent turns and revealed during Reveal stay in play face up until Clean Up (unless trashed). Two Fremen Bond cards can activate one another regardless of order, because each is the other’s “other” Fremen card. Clean Up moves them to discard.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: In play / Fremen Bond."}}

