{"q":{"id":"Q36","question":"Can Recall Agent return the Agent placed this turn, and when can the recalled Agent act again? Where does a retreated troop go, and may “retreat any number” mean zero?"},"key":{"id":"Q36","expected_answer":"Recall another Agent from board to Leader, not current-turn Agent; can use on later Agent turn same round. Retreat Conflict to garrison; any number permits zero.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1147–1157; FAQ p3 Retreat","novelty":"Recall and retreat destinations and reuse"},"A":{"id":"Q36","answer":"Recall Agent returns one of your other Agents on the board, not the Agent just placed; the recalled Agent may be used on another Agent turn in the same round. A retreated troop moves from Conflict to your garrison. “Retreat any number” may mean zero.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Recall Agent icon; Retreat; FAQ Combat and troops"},"B":{"id":"Q36","answer":"Recall Agent returns one of your other board Agents, never the one just sent; it may act again on another Agent turn that round. Retreat moves a troop from Conflict to garrison. “Retreat any number” includes zero.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Recall Agent; Retreat; FAQ: Combat and troops."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q37","question":"When an effect grants two Influence with a freely chosen Faction, may it be split? What is required for an Alliance-icon effect or a minimum-Influence effect?"},"key":{"id":"Q37","expected_answer":"Choose one Faction, both Influence there (not split). Alliance effect requires holding shown Faction Alliance token; minimum-Influence effect requires at least shown value with shown Faction.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1086–1088,1118–1126","novelty":"Effect eligibility and indivisible Influence"},"A":{"id":"Q37","answer":"A free-choice effect granting two Influence requires choosing one Faction for both; it cannot be split. An Alliance icon requires holding that Faction’s Alliance token. An effect with a minimum Influence requirement requires that level in the named Faction.","support":"supported","evidence":"Influence; Special Rules: Influence"},"B":{"id":"Q37","answer":"A free-choice gain of two Influence must go to one chosen Faction; it cannot be split. A minimum-Influence effect requires that threshold; an Alliance icon requires holding that Faction’s Alliance token.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Influence."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q38","question":"If an Alliance holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, who receives the token? If the holder drops to 3 and no one has 4, what happens?"},"key":{"id":"Q38","expected_answer":"Former holder chooses one of previously tied opponents to receive token; holder loses Alliance VP and receiver gains it. Below 4 loses token; if no eligible 4+ player return token to board, losing its VP.","source_references":"FAQ p1 Alliance","novelty":"Alliance loss from retreating holder"},"A":{"id":"Q38","answer":"If the holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, and both remain tied, the former holder chooses which tied opponent receives the Alliance. If the holder falls to 3 or lower and nobody has 4+, return the token to the board; the former holder loses its VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring: FAQ separate transfer trigger"},"B":{"id":"Q38","answer":"If holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, the former holder chooses which tied opponent receives the Alliance. If holder falls to 3 or lower and nobody has 4+, return it to the board; holder loses its Alliance VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Scoring: Faction Influence; FAQ: Alliance loss."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q39","question":"What happens to a card drawn during Reveal compared with one drawn after Reveal? What happens to a Plot Intrigue played earlier whose effect applies at Reveal?"},"key":{"id":"Q39","expected_answer":"During Reveal immediately reveal and use this turn; after Reveal keep until next round, then draw five extra. Plot effect for later Reveal stays face up until that Reveal, use then discard.","source_references":"FAQ pp2–3 Intrigue cards/Reveal turn","novelty":"Draw timing branches and delayed Plot duration"},"A":{"id":"Q39","answer":"A card drawn during Reveal is revealed immediately and used this turn; a card drawn after Reveal is kept for next round, then you draw five additional cards. A Plot Intrigue with a later Reveal effect remains face up until then, is used, then discarded.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Draw timing"},"B":{"id":"Q39","answer":"A card drawn during Reveal is immediately revealed and used this turn. A card drawn after Reveal stays for next round, in addition to the five cards then drawn. A Plot Intrigue with a later Reveal effect stays face up until then, is used, then discarded.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Draw timing."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q40","question":"May a “when you win a Conflict” Intrigue be played after tying for first? What if you receive such an Intrigue as a reward for an outright win?"},"key":{"id":"Q40","expected_answer":"Tie for first is not a win, cannot play. An appropriate Intrigue received as winning reward can be played immediately.","source_references":"FAQ p4 When you win a Conflict","novelty":"Win-trigger exception and newly gained card timing"},"A":{"id":"Q40","answer":"No. A “when you win a Conflict” Intrigue cannot be played after tying for first because nobody wins. If received as a reward for an outright win, it may be played immediately.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Combat and troops"},"B":{"id":"Q40","answer":"No; after tying for first you did not win, so a “when you win” Intrigue cannot be played. If received as a reward for an outright win, it may be played immediately.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Combat and troops."}}

