{"q":{"id":"Q41","question":"What if final VP, spice, Solari, water and garrison troops all remain tied, and may scores exceed 12?"},"key":{"id":"Q41","expected_answer":"Final tiebreaker is player who most recently took Reveal turn. Scores may exceed printed track maximum 12.","source_references":"FAQ p2 Endgame; p4 Victory Points","novelty":"Final tiebreaker and score boundary"},"A":{"id":"Q41","answer":"If VP and all listed resource tiebreakers remain tied, the player who most recently took a Reveal turn wins. Scores may exceed the printed 12 spaces.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Victory"},"B":{"id":"Q41","answer":"If VP and all four resource tiebreakers remain tied, the player who most recently took a Reveal turn wins. Scores can exceed the printed track’s 12.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Victory."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q42","question":"Can you delay completion of two held contracts for the same board space after visiting, and when in the Agent turn can their effects resolve?"},"key":{"id":"Q42","expected_answer":"Completion mandatory; all same-space contracts completed with one Agent placement. Their effects may resolve in any order with space and Agent-box effects; still must hold them at placement.","source_references":"FAQ p1 contract; Main p16","novelty":"Mandatory simultaneous contracts and effect ordering"},"A":{"id":"Q42","answer":"No. All contracts held for the same space must be fulfilled with one Agent placement; you cannot delay completion. Their effects are another effect of the Agent turn and may resolve in any order with the space and Agent-box effects, provided you held them when placing the Agent.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Contract completion is mandatory"},"B":{"id":"Q42","answer":"No; all held contracts for the same space must be fulfilled with one Agent placement. A board-space contract is another Agent-turn effect and can resolve in any order with space and Agent-box effects, but must have been held when the Agent was sent.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Contract completion is mandatory."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q43","question":"Under CHOAM does Shaddam begin with his set-aside Sardaukar contracts, when can he take one, and how long does his Signet Ring deployment restriction last?"},"key":{"id":"Q43","expected_answer":"No, not in possession at start. Sardaukar Commander allows acquiring set-aside Sardaukar contract instead of generally available one when taking a contract. Emperor of Known Universe restriction starts immediately with Signet Ring Agent placement and lasts that turn only.","source_references":"Main p17; FAQ p3 Shaddam Corrino IV","novelty":"Shaddam contract choice and restriction duration"},"A":{"id":"Q43","answer":"Shaddam does not begin with the set-aside Sardaukar contracts; only he may acquire them, choosing one instead of a public contract when acquiring a contract. His Signet restriction begins immediately when he plays Signet Ring to send an Agent and lasts for that turn only, not the whole round.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM Module: Reserved Sardaukar; Shaddam; FAQ Shaddam"},"B":{"id":"Q43","answer":"Shaddam does not start with the two reserved Sardaukar contracts; only he may acquire them, choosing one instead of a generally available contract when acquiring. Set both aside before the initial shuffle: shuffle remaining 18, reveal 2 offers, leave 16 in bank, plus 2 reserved. His Signet deployment restriction takes effect immediately and lasts for that turn only.","support":"supported","evidence":"CHOAM: Setup changes; Reserved Sardaukar contracts; FAQ: Shaddam."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q44","question":"For Feyd, where does the Training token start and what happens at its last space? Which Jessica side begins face up and can Reverend Mother Jessica act on the flip turn?"},"key":{"id":"Q44","expected_answer":"Feyd starts leftmost Training space, stays forever on rightmost once reached. Lady Jessica side starts up, not Reverend Mother. Reverend Mother ability usable on flip turn.","source_references":"Main p17 / extraction 957–964; FAQ p3 Reverend Mother Jessica","novelty":"Leader setup and transition timing"},"A":{"id":"Q44","answer":"Feyd’s token begins on the leftmost space of the Training track; when it reaches the rightmost space, it stays there. Lady Jessica begins with her Lady Jessica side face up. Reverend Mother Jessica may use her ability on the turn she flips.","support":"supported","evidence":"Leader clarifications; FAQ"},"B":{"id":"Q44","answer":"Feyd’s token starts on the leftmost Training track space and stays on the rightmost space once it reaches it. Lady Jessica side begins face up. Reverend Mother Jessica may use her ability on the turn she flips.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Leader clarifications; FAQ."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q45","question":"For Margot and Irulan does moving from 1 to 3 Influence count as reaching 2, can it trigger again later, and does descending through 2 count? Does Clean Up trigger Spacing Guild’s Favor discard ability?"},"key":{"id":"Q45","expected_answer":"Passing 2 upward counts, can repeat by losing then regaining Influence; descending does not count. Spacing Guild Favor triggers discard from hand, not in-play-to-discard Clean Up.","source_references":"Main p17 / extraction 965–978","novelty":"Threshold crossing and discard-source exception"},"A":{"id":"Q45","answer":"Yes, moving from 1 to 3 counts as reaching 2. Margot/Irulan may reach 2 with that Faction again later after losing Influence and regaining it; moving down through 2 does not count. Clean Up moving Spacing Guild’s Favor from in play to discard does not trigger its discard ability; only discarding from hand does.","support":"supported","evidence":"Leader clarifications"},"B":{"id":"Q45","answer":"Moving from 1 to 3 counts as reaching 2. It can trigger again later if you first lose Influence and then regain it by moving up; moving down through 2 does not count. Moving Spacing Guild’s Favor from in play to discard at Clean Up does not trigger its discard ability; only discarding from hand does.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Leader clarifications."}}

