{"q":{"id":"Q51","question":"What does Swordmaster cost before and after anyone obtains one, how often may each player visit, and when can the new Agent be used? Does a Rival obtaining it lower human cost?"},"key":{"id":"Q51","expected_answer":"Landsraad 8 Solari before any Swordmaster, then 6; once per player per game. Third Agent from beside board onto Leader immediately usable same round and rest of game. Rival also lowers cost.","source_references":"Supplements p2; FAQ p3 Rivals","novelty":"Swordmaster dynamic cost and immediate action capacity"},"A":{"id":"Q51","answer":"Swordmaster uses Landsraad access; it costs 8 Solari before anyone gains Swordmaster, and 6 once anyone has one. Each player may do it once per game. Take the third Agent, available this round and for the rest of the game. A Rival getting its Swordmaster also lowers human cost to 6.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q51","answer":"Swordmaster costs 8 Solari before anyone gains one, then 6; each player may gain it only once. Take the third Agent, available this round and for the rest of the game. Rival obtaining Swordmaster also lowers the human cost to 6.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide: Swordmaster."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q52","question":"State Imperial Privilege’s Agent icon, requirement, entry cost and effects. Which Agent can it recall and does it automatically give Emperor Influence?"},"key":{"id":"Q52","expected_answer":"Landsraad, 2+ Emperor Influence, 3 Solari. May discard Intrigue to draw Intrigue; recall another Agent and draw card. Not the current Agent. No automatic Emperor Influence.","source_references":"Supplements p2; Main p20","novelty":"Recall-space requirement versus Faction gain"},"A":{"id":"Q52","answer":"Imperial Privilege uses Landsraad access, costs 3 Solari and requires 2+ Emperor Influence; it is not Combat. You may discard an Intrigue to draw an Intrigue; recall one of your other Agents and draw a card. It does not automatically give Emperor Influence.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q52","answer":"Imperial Privilege is Landsraad, costs 3 Solari, requires 2+ Emperor Influence, and is not Combat. You may discard an Intrigue to draw an Intrigue; recall one of your other Agents and draw a card. It gives no automatic Emperor Influence.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide: Imperial Privilege."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q53","question":"State Shipping’s access icon, Influence requirement, cost and gains. Does its free-choice Influence have to be with the Guild?"},"key":{"id":"Q53","expected_answer":"Spice Trade, 2+ Guild Influence, 3 spice. Gain 5 Solari and one Influence any one Faction, not necessarily Guild.","source_references":"Supplements p2","novelty":"Shipping qualifying Faction versus chosen gain"},"A":{"id":"Q53","answer":"Shipping uses Spice Trade access, requires 2+ Spacing Guild Influence and costs 3 spice; it is not Combat. Gain 5 Solari and 1 Influence with any one Faction, not necessarily the Guild.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q53","answer":"Shipping is Spice Trade, requires 2+ Guild Influence and costs 3 spice; it gives 5 Solari and 1 Influence with any one Faction. The free-choice Influence need not be Guild. It is not a Combat space.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide: Shipping."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q54","question":"Compare Gather Support and Spice Refinery’s zero-cost and paid options and Combat status."},"key":{"id":"Q54","expected_answer":"Gather Support Landsraad choose 0/2 Solari, two troops either way, plus one water if paid, not Combat. Refinery City choose 0/1 spice, gain 2/4 Solari respectively, controller 1 Solari either way, Combat.","source_references":"Supplements pp1–2","novelty":"Optional entry costs and different deployment access"},"A":{"id":"Q54","answer":"Gather Support uses Landsraad access, is not Combat, and lets you choose to pay 0 or 2 Solari: recruit two troops; if you paid 2 Solari, also gain 1 water. Spice Refinery uses City access and is Combat; choose to pay 0 or 1 spice to gain respectively 2 or 4 Solari; its controller separately gains 1 Solari.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q54","answer":"Gather Support is Landsraad, non-Combat: choose to pay 0 or 2 Solari; recruit 2 troops, and if paying 2 also gain 1 water. Spice Refinery is City, Combat: choose 0 or 1 spice; gain 2 Solari free or 4 Solari if paying 1; controller separately gains 1 Solari.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q55","question":"State Heighliner, Desert Tactics and Sardaukar’s entry costs, Influence gains, recruits and other effects; which allow normal deployment?"},"key":{"id":"Q55","expected_answer":"Heighliner 5 spice, Guild Influence +1 and five troops, Combat. Desert Tactics 1 water, Fremen Influence +1 and one troop, optional trash, Combat. Sardaukar 4 spice, Emperor Influence +1 and four troops plus Intrigue, not Combat.","source_references":"Supplements pp1–2","novelty":"Faction recruit spaces with different Combat flags"},"A":{"id":"Q55","answer":"Heighliner: Spacing Guild icon, 5 spice cost, Combat yes; gain 1 Guild Influence and recruit five troops. Desert Tactics: Fremen icon, 1 water cost, Combat yes; gain 1 Fremen Influence, recruit one troop and optionally trash a card. Sardaukar: Emperor icon, 4 spice cost, Combat no; gain 1 Emperor Influence, draw an Intrigue and recruit four troops.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q55","answer":"Heighliner: Spacing Guild, costs 5 spice, gains 1 Guild Influence and recruits 5 troops; Combat yes. Desert Tactics: Fremen, costs 1 water, gains 1 Fremen Influence, recruits 1 troop, may trash a card; Combat yes. Sardaukar: Emperor, costs 4 spice, gains 1 Emperor Influence, draws an Intrigue and recruits 4 troops; Combat no.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide."}}

