{"q":{"id":"Q56","question":"What are Assembly Hall, Espionage and Deliver Supplies’s Agent icons, costs and effects, including Assembly Hall’s timing condition?"},"key":{"id":"Q56","expected_answer":"Assembly Hall Landsraad free, Intrigue now, 1 Persuasion at Reveal if own Agent there. Espionage BG 1 spice, 1 BG Influence, card and Spy. Deliver Supplies Guild free, 1 Guild Influence and 1 water. None Combat.","source_references":"Supplements p1","novelty":"Persistent location conditional and resource/spy spaces"},"A":{"id":"Q56","answer":"Assembly Hall: Landsraad icon, no cost, not Combat; draw an Intrigue and gain 1 Persuasion during your Reveal turn if your Agent is there. Espionage: Bene Gesserit icon, costs 1 spice, not Combat; gain 1 Bene Gesserit Influence, draw a card and place a Spy. Deliver Supplies: Spacing Guild icon, no cost, not Combat; gain 1 Guild Influence and 1 water.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q56","answer":"Assembly Hall: Landsraad, no cost, non-Combat; draw an Intrigue and gain 1 Persuasion during Reveal if your Agent is there. Espionage: Bene Gesserit, costs 1 spice, non-Combat; gain 1 BG Influence, draw a card, place a Spy. Deliver Supplies: Spacing Guild, no cost, non-Combat; gain 1 Guild Influence and 1 water.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q57","question":"What must False Orders’ affected opponents do, may it be played without an opposing Spy connected to your destination, and when is Litany Against Fear’s red box ignored?"},"key":{"id":"Q57","expected_answer":"Each affected opponent moves Spy to empty observation post not connected to this turn Agent destination. Can play without enemy Spy there. Litany red box ignored during Reveal or with gained Agent icon when played normally as Agent card.","source_references":"FAQ pp2–3 False Orders/Litany Against Fear","novelty":"Specific movement and card-box exceptions"},"A":{"id":"Q57","answer":"False Orders makes affected opponents move their Spy to an empty post not connected to your Agent’s destination that turn; it may be played even if no enemy Spy is connected there. Litany Against Fear’s red box is ignored during Reveal, or when it gains an Agent icon and is played as an Agent card.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: False Orders; Litany Against Fear"},"B":{"id":"Q57","answer":"False Orders makes affected opponents move their Spy to an empty post not connected to your Agent’s destination that turn; it can be played even if no enemy Spy is connected there. Litany Against Fear’s red box is ignored during Reveal, or when it gains an Agent icon and is played normally as an Agent card.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: False Orders; Litany Against Fear."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q58","question":"With Manipulate, may opponents acquire the removed card, may you acquire it by other means with the discount, and when does an unacquired card leave the game?"},"key":{"id":"Q58","expected_answer":"Opponents cannot acquire. You may use other means but 1-Persuasion discount does not apply. If not acquired by end of next Reveal turn, remove from game.","source_references":"FAQ p3 Manipulate","novelty":"Removed-row card access and expiry"},"A":{"id":"Q58","answer":"Opponents cannot acquire the card removed by Manipulate. You may acquire it by other means, but without the 1-Persuasion discount. If still unacquired at the end of your next Reveal, remove it from the game.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Manipulate"},"B":{"id":"Q58","answer":"Opponents cannot acquire the card removed by Manipulate. You may acquire it by other means without the 1-Persuasion discount. If it remains unacquired by the end of your next Reveal, remove it from the game.","support":"supported","evidence":"FAQ: Manipulate."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q60","question":"What components and resource does the standard two-player Rival start with, what happens to the 2P Reshuffle card, and can its 10 VP trigger Endgame and victory?"},"key":{"id":"Q60","expected_answer":"Four cubes at Influence bottoms, three garrison troops rest supply, two Agents supply and third beside board, three Spies and one water supply, score/Combat zero. Retain Reshuffle in Hagal. Scoring Rival can trigger end at 10+ and win.","source_references":"Supplements p3; Main p5","novelty":"Rival full setup and scoring threat"},"A":{"id":"Q60","answer":"Rival starts with four cubes at the bottom of Influence tracks, three troops in garrison and remaining troops in supply, two Agents in supply with Swordmaster beside board, three Spies, and 1 water in supply; score and Combat marker start at 0. Shuffle House Hagal near the Rival and retain the 2P Reshuffle card. Its 10+ VP triggers Endgame and it can win.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup"},"B":{"id":"Q60","answer":"Rival starts with 3 troops in garrison and remaining troops in supply, 2 Agents in supply and Swordmaster beside board, 3 Spies, 1 water, and score/Combat markers at 0. Shuffle House Hagal retaining the 2P Reshuffle card. Rival at 10+ VP triggers Endgame and can win.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q61","question":"When does a Rival buy Swordmaster, how does it count and prioritize spending resources, does it keep leftovers, and is its Agent available immediately?"},"key":{"id":"Q61","expected_answer":"As soon as total resources reaches printed value; Solari spice Intrigues water each unit one. Spend only threshold, prioritizing Solari then spice then Intrigue then water; keep leftovers. Third Agent immediately available including current round.","source_references":"Supplements p5; p2 Swordmaster; FAQ p3 Rivals","novelty":"Automated mixed-resource upgrade timing"},"A":{"id":"Q61","answer":"When its total resources reach its printed Swordmaster value, spend exactly that amount and take its third Agent, usable in the current round. Count all Solari, spice, Intrigue cards and water in supply, each one counting as one, including starting water. Mandatory spend order: Solari, spice, Intrigue cards, then water; keep leftovers after paying the value. The Agent is immediately usable.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Swordmaster resource total and spending priority"},"B":{"id":"Q61","answer":"As soon as its Solari, spice, Intrigue cards, and water total reaches printed Swordmaster value (each unit/card counts 1), spend exactly that amount in mandatory order: Solari, spice, Intrigue, water. Keep leftovers. Take its third Agent for immediate use this round.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Swordmaster resource total."}}

