{"q":{"id":"Q62","question":"After a Rival has Swordmaster, which exact resource sets does it spend for VP, and can it spend a mixed total of seven resources for a VP?"},"key":{"id":"Q62","expected_answer":"Each set 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigues or 3 water gives 1 VP whenever available. No mixed seven-resource VP purchase; mixed total only used for Swordmaster.","source_references":"Supplements p5 Buying Victory Points diagram","novelty":"Rival homogeneous conversion thresholds"},"A":{"id":"Q62","answer":"After Swordmaster, spend each exact set of 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigue cards or 3 water for 1 VP. Mixed resource totals do not qualify; it cannot spend a mixed seven for VP.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: After Swordmaster"},"B":{"id":"Q62","answer":"After Swordmaster, spend 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigue cards, or 3 water for 1 VP per set. Mixed totals do not qualify.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: After Swordmaster."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q63","question":"When choosing Influence, how does a Rival select the Faction and break ties? Does it get VP at 2 and Alliance VP, or the track bonus at 4? What does a numbered Hagal Influence icon mean?"},"key":{"id":"Q63","expected_answer":"Choose least Influence, ties leftmost priority. Gains/losses of Influence VP and Alliance VP as humans, no 4-track bonus. Number means Faction at that position in printed priority list.","source_references":"Supplements pp4–5; Main p7","novelty":"Rival priority and track-bonus exception"},"A":{"id":"Q63","answer":"Rival chooses the Faction with least Influence, breaking ties by leftmost priority icon. It gains VP at 2 Influence and Alliance VP as a human does, but not the 4-Influence track bonus. A numbered Hagal Influence icon means that position in its Rival card’s Faction priority list.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Influence; resource gains"},"B":{"id":"Q63","answer":"Choose the Faction with least Influence, breaking ties by leftmost priority icon. Rival gains/losses VP at 2 Influence and gains/loses Alliance VP like a human, but does not receive 4-Influence track bonuses. A numbered Hagal Influence icon means that position in the Rival card’s Faction priority list.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: After Swordmaster; Agent turns."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q64","question":"A Rival reveals a two-destination Hagal card and the condition-selected destination is occupied. Can it use the other destination, and what conditions select these cards?"},"key":{"id":"Q64","expected_answer":"Cannot switch to other; reveal again. Accept Contract/Shipping based on Guild Influence; Deliver Supplies/Heighliner based on Conflict tier I/II/III. Use card printed condition.","source_references":"Supplements p4 Special Instructions; FAQ p3 Rivals","novelty":"Rival conditional destination cannot fallback"},"A":{"id":"Q64","answer":"No. For a two-destination card, use only the condition-matching destination; if that destination is occupied, reveal another Hagal card without using the other destination. Conditions are Guild Influence for Accept Contract/Shipping, and Conflict tier for Deliver Supplies/Heighliner.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns"},"B":{"id":"Q64","answer":"No. With a two-destination card, choose only the destination matching current conditions (Guild Influence for Accept Contract/Shipping; Conflict tier for Deliver Supplies/Heighliner); if it is occupied, reveal a new card without using the other destination.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q65","question":"A Rival has no troops newly recruited by a card sending it to Combat. Can it deploy garrison troops? What if a Hagal card recruits at a noncombat space or has a conditional 2-Influence bonus not met?"},"key":{"id":"Q65","expected_answer":"Still deploy up to two available garrison troops at Combat. New troops at noncombat go garrison. Missing 2-Influence bonus does not block placement, just no bonus. Use only Hagal effects, not ordinary board effects.","source_references":"Supplements p4","novelty":"Rival deployment and conditional bonus failure"},"A":{"id":"Q65","answer":"Yes, at every Combat space the Rival deploys up to two available garrison troops, even if the card recruited none. At a noncombat space recruited troops go into its garrison. A conditional 2+ Influence bonus not met does not prevent Agent placement; just omit that bonus.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns"},"B":{"id":"Q65","answer":"Yes. At any Combat space deploy up to 2 available garrison troops even if the card recruited none; newly recruited troops deploy too. At a noncombat space recruited troops go to garrison. A conditional 2+ Influence bonus is simply omitted if unmet; it never blocks placement.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q66","question":"How does a Rival choose an unrestricted Spy post, what happens if all Faction posts are occupied, and what occurs on placing its third Spy? Can it Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?"},"key":{"id":"Q66","expected_answer":"First available Faction post by priority; if all full ignore placement. Third/final supply Spy placed triggers immediately recalling other two and printed Scheme. Never Infiltrate/Gather Intelligence.","source_references":"Supplements pp4–5","novelty":"Rival automated spy placement and Scheme trigger"},"A":{"id":"Q66","answer":"Unless specified, choose the first available Faction observation post in priority order. If all four are occupied, ignore placement. Placing its third/final supply Spy immediately recalls its other two Spies and triggers Scheme. Rivals never recall Spies to Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Spies and Schemes"},"B":{"id":"Q66","answer":"Unless specified, put a Spy at first available Faction post in priority order; if all four are occupied, ignore placement. Placing third/final supply Spy recalls the other two and triggers Scheme. Rival never recalls Spies for Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Spies and Schemes."}}

