{"q":{"id":"Q67","question":"If a Rival’s Scheme recruits troops before a Hagal Agent reaches a Combat space on that same turn, what happens to those troops? What if a Place Spy card found no legal post?"},"key":{"id":"Q67","expected_answer":"Deploy Scheme recruits on same-turn Combat placement. Place Spy card still followed by another Hagal reveal whether placement succeeds or not, because no Agent has been sent.","source_references":"Supplements pp4–5","novelty":"Scheme recruitment timing before placement"},"A":{"id":"Q67","answer":"If Scheme recruits before placement and the Rival visits a Combat space that turn, deploy those newly recruited troops too. If Place Spy finds no empty post of the required type, ignore the placement, then immediately reveal another Hagal card and continue the Agent turn.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Agent turns; Spies and Schemes"},"B":{"id":"Q67","answer":"Scheme-recruited troops can deploy if the Rival visits a Combat space that same turn. A Place Spy card with no legal post is ignored, but Rival immediately reveals another Hagal card and continues because it has not placed an Agent.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Spies and Schemes."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q68","question":"At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert, how does a Rival choose worms versus base spice with Hooks, without Hooks, or with a protected Conflict? What happens to accumulated bonus spice?"},"key":{"id":"Q68","expected_answer":"Always take bonus spice. With Hooks and summonable Conflict summons one at Hagga/two Deep instead of base. Without Hooks or if protected, summons none and gains base spice (2/4). At Imperial Basin gains base1. Hagal wall removal requires Hooks.","source_references":"Supplements p5; p4 icons","novelty":"Rival mandatory worm choice and fallback"},"A":{"id":"Q68","answer":"The Rival always takes all bonus spice at a visited Maker space. At Hagga Basin/Deep Desert, if it has Hooks and the Conflict permits worms, it summons one/two worms instead of base spice; if it summons none, it takes base spice (2/4). Without Hooks, or if worms are prohibited by the Wall, it takes base spice. Hooks are not spent.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Maker spaces"},"B":{"id":"Q68","answer":"At Hagga/Deep Desert, Rival collects all bonus spice. With Hooks and a Conflict permitting worms, summon one at Hagga or two at Deep Desert instead of base spice; if it summons none, take base spice (2/4). Thus without Hooks, or at protected Conflict, take base spice.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Maker spaces."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q69","question":"When and how is a Rival’s Combat strength bonus determined, what if Reshuffle appears, and can humans respond afterward? Does a unit-free Rival get this bonus?"},"key":{"id":"Q69","expected_answer":"Start Combat in turn order, only with deployed unit: one Hagal card, bottom swords only added. Reshuffle and draw again on Reshuffle. Humans then Combat Intrigue before resolution. No unit no bonus.","source_references":"Supplements p5 Combat","novelty":"Automated bonus precedes human response"},"A":{"id":"Q69","answer":"At Combat start, if the Rival has at least one unit deployed, reveal one Hagal card in turn order and add only its bottom swords to strength. If Reshuffle appears, reshuffle and reveal again. Then humans have their normal Combat Intrigue window. A Rival with no deployed unit gets no bonus.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Combat"},"B":{"id":"Q69","answer":"At Combat start, if Rival has at least one unit deployed, reveal one Hagal card and add its bottom swords; on Reshuffle reshuffle and reveal again. Humans then get their normal Combat Intrigue window. Unit-free Rival receives no bonus.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Combat."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q70","question":"Can a Rival gain control, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and doubled rewards? How does it handle optional Conflict VP payments and contract rewards with CHOAM?"},"key":{"id":"Q70","expected_answer":"Normal control visit bonus and defensive supply troop; win card/match icons; sandworms double. Always buy optional Conflict VP if can pay resources or required Spy recall. Never contracts; each contract reward becomes 2 Solari even with CHOAM.","source_references":"Supplements p5 Combat","novelty":"Rival reward choices and module exception"},"A":{"id":"Q70","answer":"Yes: Rival gains control, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and sandworm-doubled rewards normally. It always takes optional Conflict VP if it can pay resources or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts; a contract reward gives it 2 Solari even with CHOAM.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Combat"},"B":{"id":"Q70","answer":"Yes: Rival gets control and defensive troop bonuses, battle-icon VP, and doubles rewards with worms; it wins cards normally. Always take optional Conflict VP if it can pay or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts: a contract reward gives 2 Solari even with CHOAM.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Combat."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q71","question":"When during Reveal do you total, announce and set Combat strength, can you update it during the turn, and how is strength over 20 marked?"},"key":{"id":"Q71","expected_answer":"After Reveal Cards and before Clean Up, at any point while resolving effects; announce total, set marker and update as needed. Above20 flip +20 side and count again from beginning of track.","source_references":"Main pp12–13 / extraction 652–665,733–738","novelty":"Flexible strength-setting timing and marker overflow"},"A":{"id":"Q71","answer":"During Reveal effects, total/announce strength and set the Combat marker at any point, updating it as needed. If strength exceeds 20, flip marker to +20 side and start again from the beginning of track.","support":"supported","evidence":"Reveal Turn; Strength"},"B":{"id":"Q71","answer":"Total, announce and set strength during Reveal resolution, at any point; update as needed while resolving. If over 20, flip marker to +20 side and start again from the track beginning.","support":"supported","evidence":"Reveal Turn; Actions: Strength."}}

