{"q":{"id":"Q72","question":"When is a Leader’s Signet Ring ability activated, does merely revealing Signet Ring activate it, and can card text override normal game rules?"},"key":{"id":"Q72","expected_answer":"Activated when playing Signet Ring on an Agent turn, not when merely revealing. Left Leader ability used as described. Cards of any type can override normal rules.","source_references":"Main p6,p20 / extraction 306–310,327–329,1162–1164","novelty":"Generic Signet trigger and rules precedence"},"A":{"id":"Q72","answer":"A human Leader’s Signet Ring ability activates when you play Signet Ring on one of your Agent turns, not merely when revealed. Card text may override usual game rules.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup; Overview"},"B":{"id":"Q72","answer":"Leader’s Signet ability activates when Signet Ring is played to send an Agent on an Agent turn, not merely revealed. Cards may override normal game rules.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, step 3; Overview."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q73","question":"How is a Recall Spy icon on a card resolved, where does the Spy go, and is it automatically the same as Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?"},"key":{"id":"Q73","expected_answer":"Return one of own Spies from observation post to supply, usually a cost for card effect. Card recall distinct from the two voluntary recalls for Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; it does not automatically give either benefit.","source_references":"Main p11,p20 / extraction 603–605,1150–1151","novelty":"Card recall destination versus voluntary recall purpose"},"A":{"id":"Q73","answer":"A Recall Spy icon returns one of your Spies from an observation post to your supply, usually as a cost for an effect. It does not by itself mean Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those abilities have their own effects and timing.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Spies & observation posts; Infiltrate/Gather Intelligence"},"B":{"id":"Q73","answer":"Recall Spy icon returns one of your Spies from a post to your supply, usually as a cost. It is not inherently Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those effects specify what the recall accomplishes.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Spies & observation posts; Recall Spy icon."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q74","question":"What does the “trash an Intrigue” icon allow you to choose, as opposed to an ordinary discard-a-card instruction?"},"key":{"id":"Q74","expected_answer":"Trash an Intrigue of choice from own hand. Ordinary discard chooses a non-Intrigue from hand unless explicitly specified.","source_references":"Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1184","novelty":"Dedicated Intrigue trash versus ordinary deck discard"},"A":{"id":"Q74","answer":"Trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. An ordinary discard instruction instead discards a chosen card from your hand, and cannot be an Intrigue unless specified.","support":"supported","evidence":"Trashing; Discarding"},"B":{"id":"Q74","answer":"The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand; an ordinary discard instruction discards from your hand and cannot discard Intrigue unless specified.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Trashing; Discarding."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q75","question":"A Conflict reward grants one Influence of your choice and is doubled by your sandworm. May the two gains go to different Factions? Contrast a single effect that grants two Influence."},"key":{"id":"Q75","expected_answer":"Yes. Sandworm doubling of a one-Influence reward gives two separate gains, which may use the same Faction or two different Factions. A single two-Influence effect instead chooses just one Faction and cannot be split.","source_references":"Main PDF p14 Sandworm Reward Doubling example and p20 Influence icons / extraction 778–791,1123–1126","novelty":"Explicit doubled-reward Influence split exception versus indivisible two-Influence effect"},"A":{"id":"Q75","answer":"When sandworm doubling applies to a Conflict reward granting 1 Influence, the reward is received twice, and the two gains may go to the same Faction or different Factions. Contrast a single effect granting two free-choice Influence: both must go to one Faction.","support":"supported","evidence":"Sandworm Reward Doubling; Influence"},"B":{"id":"Q75","answer":"Doubling a one-Influence reward yields 2 Influence; because reward doubling permits the optional reward to be taken a second time, you may choose the same Faction or two different Factions. A single effect granting 2 Influence with free choice must put both in one Faction.","support":"supported","evidence":"Sandworm Reward Doubling; Special Rules: Influence."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q76","question":"A House Hagal card shows a Signet Ring effect for the two-player Rival. Which ability is resolved, and does the Rival need a human Signet Ring card or a Reveal turn to trigger it?"},"key":{"id":"Q76","expected_answer":"Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the selected Rival card as the Hagal effect. No human deck Signet Ring card or Reveal turn is involved; Rival never Reveals.","source_references":"Supplements PDF pp3–4 Rival card anatomy and House Hagal Signet Ring icon","novelty":"Rival Hagal Signet trigger distinct from human Signet Ring Agent-card trigger"},"A":{"id":"Q76","answer":"Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the Rival card, not its Scheme. It is triggered by the Hagal Signet Ring effect; no human Signet Ring card or Rival Reveal turn is involved.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Rival Signet Ring and Scheme"},"B":{"id":"Q76","answer":"Resolve the Rival card’s printed Signet Ring ability. Do not substitute Scheme. It is triggered by the Hagal Signet Ring effect; no human Signet Ring card or Reveal turn is involved.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Rival Signet Ring and Scheme."}}

