{"q":{"id":"Q77","question":"For a two-player Rival, what do House Hagal Maker Hooks and Shield Wall removal icons do if it already has Hooks, lacks Hooks, or the wall is already gone?"},"key":{"id":"Q77","expected_answer":"Maker Hooks icon takes a token onto garrison only if Rival lacks one. Shield Wall removal effect removes the wall if Rival has Hooks and wall remains; without Hooks ignore the removal effect, and if wall already gone no wall remains to remove.","source_references":"Supplements PDF p4 Hagal icon explanations","novelty":"Rival-only prerequisite on wall removal, and idempotent Hooks acquisition"},"A":{"id":"Q77","answer":"Hagal Maker Hooks takes one token if the Rival lacks Hooks; if it already has Hooks, take none. Shield Wall removal removes the Wall only if Rival has Hooks and Wall remains; without Hooks or when Wall is already gone, ignore it.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Rival Hooks and Wall icons"},"B":{"id":"Q77","answer":"Maker Hooks effect takes one token if Rival lacks one; if it already has Hooks, take none. Wall removal works only if Rival has Hooks and Wall remains; without Hooks ignore it, and if Wall is already gone it has no effect.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Rival Hooks and Wall icons."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q78","question":"For Secrets, state its Agent icon, entry cost, Combat status and all effects, including which Intrigues come from the deck and which come from opponents."},"key":{"id":"Q78","expected_answer":"Bene Gesserit, no cost, not Combat. Gain one BG Influence and draw one Intrigue from deck. Each opponent with four or more Intrigues gives one randomly selected Intrigue; below four gives none.","source_references":"Supplements PDF p2 Secrets; Main p7 Intrigue and p20 Steal Intrigue","novelty":"Complete Secrets space procedure; prior Q32 asks only theft selection, not separate deck draw/Influence/access/Combat status"},"A":{"id":"Q78","answer":"Secrets uses Bene Gesserit access, no cost, not Combat. Gain 1 Bene Gesserit Influence and draw an Intrigue from the Intrigue deck; additionally, each opponent with 4+ Intrigues gives one selected at random.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide"},"B":{"id":"Q78","answer":"Secrets is Bene Gesserit, no cost, non-Combat; gain 1 BG Influence and draw an Intrigue from the deck. Each opponent with 4+ Intrigues also gives one selected at random.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide: Secrets; Intrigue cards."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q79","question":"For Imperial Basin, state its Agent icon, entry cost and Combat status, how much base and bonus spice the visiting player receives, and what its controller receives if that same player controls it."},"key":{"id":"Q79","expected_answer":"Spice Trade, no entry cost, Combat. Visitor gains one base spice plus all accumulated bonus spice. Controller gains one additional spice whenever anyone visits, including self; a controlling visitor receives both gains.","source_references":"Supplements PDF p2 Imperial Basin; Main p10 control","novelty":"Imperial Basin base-spice procedure, plus self-controller benefit; prior Maker and control questions never request this complete visit outcome"},"A":{"id":"Q79","answer":"Imperial Basin uses Spice Trade access, no cost, Combat yes. Visitor gains 1 base spice plus all bonus spice there; controller gains 1 spice. If the visitor controls it, that player receives both visitor gains and controller bonus.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide; controller/visitor rule"},"B":{"id":"Q79","answer":"Imperial Basin is Spice Trade, no cost, Combat yes; visitor receives 1 base spice plus all bonus spice. Its controller separately gets 1 spice, so if visitor controls it that player gets both effects.","support":"supported","evidence":"Board Space Guide: Imperial Basin."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q80","question":"At Round Start, where is the newly revealed Conflict placed, what happens to any unclaimed Conflict card left from earlier rounds, and does each player draw the round’s five cards before or after revealing the Conflict?"},"key":{"id":"Q80","expected_answer":"Reveal top Conflict face up in space next to deck, on top of any Conflict cards still there from earlier rounds. Then each player draws five; card not won in previous round is not taken into a player supply by this placement.","source_references":"Main PDF p8 / extraction 355–360","novelty":"Current/unclaimed Conflict card destination and replacement order, previously only key background in Q23"},"A":{"id":"Q80","answer":"At Round Start, reveal a new Conflict from the top and place it face up next to the deck, on top of any unclaimed Conflict cards from prior rounds; resolve defensive troop bonus, then each player draws five cards.","support":"supported","evidence":"Round Start"},"B":{"id":"Q80","answer":"Reveal a new Conflict from top of deck and place it face up next to/on top of any unclaimed Conflict cards remaining from earlier rounds. Then resolve defensive bonus; after that each player draws 5.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 1: Round Start."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q81","question":"At standard human setup, where do the four Faction Influence cubes and Alliance tokens begin, does anyone start with an Alliance, and is the Shield Wall initially present?"},"key":{"id":"Q81","expected_answer":"Each human puts one cube at bottom of each of four Influence tracks, starting at zero Influence. Alliance tokens are on their marked track spaces, not held by players; nobody starts allied. Shield Wall starts present in marked area below Spice Refinery, protecting its three locations until removed.","source_references":"Main PDF pp4–5 and p10 / extraction 239–246,274–278,506–522","novelty":"Initial unclaimed Alliances/zero human Influence and initially active protection, distinct from later threshold/transfer questions"},"A":{"id":"Q81","answer":"Each human places one cube at the bottom of each of the four Faction tracks. Four Alliance tokens start on marked areas of the four tracks; no human starts with one. Shield Wall token begins in its marked area below Spice Refinery.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup"},"B":{"id":"Q81","answer":"Each player puts one cube at the bottom of each of four Influence tracks; Alliance tokens start on marked areas of those tracks, so nobody starts holding one. Shield Wall token is placed on the marked area below Spice Refinery.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, steps 1 and 6."}}

