{"q":{"id":"Q82","question":"In a normal three- or four-player round, who takes the first Player Turn, how does turn order proceed after someone Reveals, and exactly when does Player Turns end? During Combat Intrigue, who has first priority, in which direction does priority proceed, and how many Combat Intrigues may an eligible player play before yielding?"},"key":{"id":"Q82","expected_answer":"Player Turns starts with the First Player marker and proceeds clockwise one turn at a time. Skip anyone who has already Revealed; the phase ends when all players have Revealed. Combat Intrigue likewise begins with First Player and proceeds clockwise among players with at least one unit in the Conflict; each may play any number or pass.","source_references":"Main PDF pp8,14; run extraction lines397–459,813–826","novelty":"Turn priority, skipped players and phase termination are not requested by Q03/Q08/Q23; Q19 only asks the two-player Rival order. Any-number Combat permission is also unasked."},"A":{"id":"Q82","answer":"First Player starts and turns continue clockwise, one turn at a time; a player who Reveals is skipped thereafter. In 3–4 player play, Player Turns ends when all players have Revealed. During Combat Intrigue, First Player starts and priority continues clockwise; each eligible player may play any number or pass, and the window closes after involved players pass consecutively.","support":"supported","evidence":"Turn Structure: Player Turns; Combat"},"B":{"id":"Q82","answer":"First Player acts first, then clockwise; players continue taking one turn at a time. A Revealed player skips remaining turns; phase ends when all players Revealed. Combat Intrigue starts with First Player, proceeds clockwise; eligible players may play any number before passing.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 2: Player Turns; Phase 3: Combat."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q83","question":"What are the three steps of a Reveal turn, in order? Must the Reveal-box effects be resolved in card order, or may the player choose their order?"},"key":{"id":"Q83","expected_answer":"Reveal Cards, Resolve Reveal Effects, Clean Up, in that order. Reveal all remaining hand cards first; resolve their Reveal effects in any chosen order; then clean up all played cards.","source_references":"Main PDF p12; run extraction lines714–748","novelty":"Q03 asks card eligibility/destination, Q13 purchase interleaving and Q71 strength timing; none requests the Reveal step sequence or effect-order freedom."},"A":{"id":"Q83","answer":"Reveal turn: (1) reveal all remaining hand cards; (2) resolve their Reveal box effects, in any order, spend Persuasion and set Combat strength; (3) Clean Up all cards in front of you to discard. Effects need not resolve in card order.","support":"supported","evidence":"Reveal Turn"},"B":{"id":"Q83","answer":"Reveal Cards; Resolve Reveal Effects; Clean Up. Reveal effects may be resolved in any order.","support":"supported","evidence":"Reveal Turn."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q84","question":"Before the first round without CHOAM, how are each human starter deck, Intrigue deck, Imperium deck/Row and Reserve stacks prepared? Where do the human Combat marker, three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start?"},"key":{"id":"Q84","expected_answer":"Each human shuffles their identical ten-card starting deck and puts it face down in their supply left of their Leader. Omit CHOAM-marked Imperium/Intrigue cards, shuffle the Intrigue and Imperium decks face down, deal five Imperium cards face up, and place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks next to the Row. Human Combat marker starts at zero on the indicated initial side; three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start in their supply in clear view.","source_references":"Main PDF pp3–5; run extraction lines102–319, especially C1–C3/E/G3/G6","novelty":"Initial deck/market preparation and the remaining human component destinations are not requested by Q01/Q02/Q16/Q21/Q60/Q81. These establish playable initial state; not a numerical variant of an existing setup question."},"A":{"id":"Q84","answer":"Without CHOAM omit CHOAM-marked cards, shuffle each human 10-card starter and place it face down in supply; shuffle Intrigue and Imperium decks separately, face down; deal five face up to Imperium Row; place Prepare the Way and Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks. Human Combat marker starts at 0; three Spies, Councilor and three Control markers start in personal supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup; Initial card states; Human component layout"},"B":{"id":"Q84","answer":"Shuffle each human’s 10-card starter and place face down in supply. Omit CHOAM cards (including from both decks); shuffle Intrigue and Imperium decks separately face down; deal 5 face up to Imperium Row; place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate stacks. Combat marker starts at 0; three Spies, Councilor, and all three Control markers start in personal supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, steps 4 and 6; Human component layout."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q85","question":"Which cards may you ordinarily acquire with Persuasion, where is each acquisition cost shown, and during which kind of your turn may you make those ordinary Persuasion purchases?"},"key":{"id":"Q85","expected_answer":"During the player’s Reveal turn, acquire any available card from the five-card Imperium Row or Prepare the Way/The Spice Must Flow from the Reserve, paying the Persuasion cost printed at the top right. Ordinary Persuasion purchasing is a Reveal-turn procedure.","source_references":"Main PDF p13 Acquiring Cards and p20 Persuasion; run extraction lines775–806,1256–1259","novelty":"Q13 asks spending within Reveal, pooling, replacement and destination; it does not ask the legal purchase sources, printed price or whether an Agent turn permits ordinary purchases. Q34 only asks acquire-box/reshuffle rules."},"A":{"id":"Q85","answer":"During a Reveal turn, spend Persuasion to acquire any of five Imperium Row cards or either Reserve card (Prepare the Way or The Spice Must Flow). Cost is at top right. Ordinary Persuasion purchases are made during Reveal, not Agent turn.","support":"supported","evidence":"Acquiring Cards"},"B":{"id":"Q85","answer":"Ordinarily buy any of five Imperium Row cards or Reserve Prepare the Way / The Spice Must Flow; cost appears at top right. These Persuasion purchases occur during Reveal turn.","support":"supported","evidence":"Acquiring Cards."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q86","question":"When a human receives a Spy placement icon or a Recall Spy icon, may the player decline the action even if a legal Spy/post exists? Does a Shield Wall destruction icon require destruction, and if destroyed can the Wall return in a later round?"},"key":{"id":"Q86","expected_answer":"Ordinary Spy placement and ordinary Recall Spy are permissive: may place/recall. An unpaid optional recall cost gives no associated benefit; Intrigue costs/conditions still must be met to play that Intrigue. Shield Wall destruction is optional. Once removed, return it to the box; it is gone for the rest of the game.","source_references":"Main PDF pp10–11; FAQ pp3–4 optional effects/Shield Wall; run main lines577–585,646–665; FAQ lines217–228,304–306","novelty":"Q26 asks placement legality, Q73 asks recall resolution/destination and Q49 asks Sietch option outcomes, but none expressly requests these human icon optionality branches or Wall permanence. Q77 is Rival-specific and uses different mandatory automation."},"A":{"id":"Q86","answer":"Yes, ordinary human Spy placement and Recall Spy icons are optional even when legal. Shield Wall destruction is optional (“may remove”); once removed it is returned to the box and cannot return later.","support":"supported","evidence":"Spies & observation posts; Shield Wall"},"B":{"id":"Q86","answer":"Yes, ordinary Spy placement and Recall Spy icons are optional even with a legal placement/recall. Shield Wall removal is optional; once removed it is returned to box and cannot return later.","support":"supported","evidence":"Special Rules: Spies & observation posts; Shield Wall; FAQ: Mandatory effects."}}

