{"q":{"id":"Q97","question":"Before the first round of standard two-player play, how do you prepare the House Hagal deck and where do you put it? Is its 2P Reshuffle card removed?"},"key":{"id":"Q97","expected_answer":"Shuffle the House Hagal deck and place it near the shared Rival. Keep the card marked 2P Reshuffle in that deck; removing it is a solo-game instruction.","source_references":[{"file":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt","lines":[199,200],"pdf":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/source_pdfs/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.pdf","pdf_page":3}],"novelty":"Q20 asks only what happens after the House Hagal deck is empty or Reshuffle is drawn. Q60 asks starting Rival personal components/resources and what happens to the 2P Reshuffle card, not preparation of the shared deck. Q84 explicitly enumerates human starter, Intrigue, Imperium/Row and Reserve setup and does not include House Hagal. None of the remaining complete-bank questions requests the initial House Hagal shuffle. This is a source-prescribed initial state for the distinct automation mechanism, not a changed destination/resource/number in an existing visit or reward branch. The retained 2P card is repeated here only to make the setup answer complete, and is not claimed as new coverage."},"A":{"id":"Q97","answer":"Shuffle House Hagal and place the deck near the shared Rival, retaining the 2P Reshuffle card.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup"},"B":{"id":"Q97","answer":"Shuffle House Hagal and place deck near shared Rival, retaining the 2P Reshuffle card.","support":"supported","evidence":"Required Rival Rules: Setup."}}
