trength, during the Combat Intrigue window. Reveal strength is not fixed; use the adjusted strength shown on the track to resolve Combat.","support":"supported","evidence":"Combat: Combat Intrigue"},"B":{"id":"Q99","answer":"Yes, adjust the Combat marker when the Combat Intrigue resolves during the Combat Intrigue window. The Reveal-turn total is not fixed; use adjusted strength shown on track to resolve rewards.","support":"supported","evidence":"Phase 3: Combat."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q100","question":"When an ordinary effect tells you to gain Solari, spice or water, where do the gained resource tokens come from? May you take them from another player’s supply instead?"},"key":{"id":"Q100","expected_answer":"Take ordinary resource gains from the common bank. Do not take them from another player’s supply.","source_references":[{"file":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt","pdf_page":20,"lines":[1281,1283]},{"file":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt","pdf_page":20,"lines":[1171,1173]}],"novelty":"Accept exactly one grouped question for the single general resource-gain origin rule. Do not create separate Solari, spice and water variants. This is not a changed amount/name within a tested branch: an ordinary gain from the bank leaves opponents’ holdings intact, whereas taking from another player changes two players’ holdings. The source explicitly defines that legal origin. Q22’s correct incidental key clause cannot substitute for an actual requested question part."},"A":{"id":"Q100","answer":"Gained Solari, spice or water comes from the bank. You do not take it from another player’s supply.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup: bank rule"},"B":{"id":"Q100","answer":"Gained Solari, spice, or water come from the bank, not another player’s supply; payments return to bank.","support":"supported","evidence":"Setup, step 7."}}
{"q":{"id":"Q101","question":"When setting up standard CHOAM with the 20 standard contracts, how must the contract tokens be prepared before the two face-up offers are exposed? May players choose the offers or preset the order of the face-down bank instead?"},"key":{"id":"Q101","expected_answer":"Shuffle the 20 standard contracts face down, then flip two face up onto the marked board spaces beneath the Landsraad Council. Put the remaining 18 face down in the bank. The offers and bank order come from that shuffled supply, rather than player selection or a preset order. This is the generic module setup; any Leader instruction about set-aside contracts is resolved as that instruction directs.","source_references":[{"file":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt","lines":[936,944],"pdf_pages":[16]},{"file":"/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt","lines":[853,861],"pdf_pages":[16]}],"novelty":"Q16 requests the face-up and face-down counts, additional cards, optional Shaddam and exclusion of the 10 Ix tokens, but does not request initial shuffling/randomization. Q17 requests taking/refilling an existing contract display, Q18/Q42 request completion, and Q43 requests Shaddam possession/acquisition and Signet timing. Q84 explicitly requests non-CHOAM human/deck setup, and Q97 explicitly requests the distinct House Hagal deck. No question asks for preparing the randomized CHOAM contract supply. The claim is only the previously unrequested shuffle rule, which determines the identity/order of available contracts; the already tested counts and placements are repeated solely to make the answer usable. This is a separate source-prescribed initial state, not altered numbers or names within a visit/reward branch."},"A":{"id":"Q101","answer":"Shuffle the 20 standard contract tokens face down, then flip two face up as offers and leave the rest